PROPOSITIONS:
<s>
- Weight-loss pens.
</s>
<s>
- Have you ever used one?
- Do you know someone who has used one?
</s>
<s>
- Today, more than half of Brazilians are overweight.
- Today, more than half of Brazilians have an associated comorbidity.
- Around 20% of Brazilians are already in the obesity range.
</s>
<s>
- These medications are intended precisely for these people.
- These medications are commonly known as weight-loss pens.
</s>
<s>
- Three of these medications are approved in Brazil.
- liraglutide is approved in Brazil.
- sold under the brand name Saxenda.
- semaglutide is approved in Brazil.
- known as Wegovy.
- known as Ozempic.
- tirzepatide is approved in Brazil.
- sold as Mounjaro.
</s>
<s>
- When you gain weight, your body does everything it can to maintain the weight you have gained.
</s>
<s>
- It does not matter how much you exercise.
- It does not matter how little you eat.
</s>
<s>
- When you take the medication, you feel less hungry.
- When you take the medication, you become full more quickly.
</s>
<s>
- The medication is like a kick-start.
- The treatment is much more complex than that.
</s>
<s>
- The problem is that medication alone is not enough.
</s>
<s>
- You need to change your lifestyle as a whole by adjusting your diet.
- You need to change your lifestyle as a whole by exercising.
</s>
<s>
- After all, obesity is a chronic disease.
- obesity is a chronic disease like diabetes.
- obesity is a chronic disease like hypertension.
</s>
<s>
- Even after losing weight, you will not be cured.
- Even after losing weight, you may regain weight at any time.
</s>
<s>
- The assessment of which medication is most appropriate for your case must be individualized.
- The assessment of which medication is most appropriate for your case must be performed by a physician.
</s>
<s>
- These medications are sold only with a prescription.
- These medications are sold only to protect your health.
</s>
<s>
- Improper use without medical guidance can cause adverse effects.
</s>
<s>
- People who seek treatment on their own may experience unpleasant side effects.
- People who seek treatment on their own may experience drug interactions.
- People who seek treatment on their own may experience excessive loss of muscle mass.
- People who seek treatment on their own may experience sarcopenia.
- People who seek treatment on their own may experience hair loss.
- People who seek treatment on their own may experience brittle nails.
- People who seek treatment on their own may experience malnutrition.
- People who seek treatment on their own may experience pancreatic toxicity.
- People who seek treatment on their own may experience the risk of obtaining counterfeit medications.
</s>
<s>
- In other words, in the long term, you may lose weight.
- In other words, in the long term, you may lose your health.
</s>
<s>
- These medications can help people who need them.
- The goal is not to help you lose a few pounds for aesthetic reasons.
- The goal is to restore health.
- The goal is to restore quality of life.
</s>